"Later, Stella joins Nathan Lark as one of the Heirs and swears their oath on the Gemore Seal."
"Later, her first wizardry burns Litcliff's palace, nearly destroying the city."
"Later, she names her spell hydrabane, hungry purple fire, after killing a hydra eel with it."
"Later, her [Fly] spell drops Aarl a hundred feet onto rocks."
"Later, she and Nathan write the Liber Physicae, a book of Earth science with a periodic table."
"Later, deep Insights give her electricity and light mana, and she casts lasers."
"Later, Brox imposes a mental skill on her, and she distrusts him for it."
"Years later she is level 729 and learns wizardry from Ushia; her wizard flame burns dark purple."
"Nathan teaches her fusion and fission; she swears on her magic to nuke only the mightiest foes."
"She casts her first fusion spell in the mountains of Esebus."
"In Esebus a laser reflected by Sussu burns through her shoulder and lung."
"She takes a Kalis wizard-staff of silvery cubes from Sussu's vault that copies her spells."
"Badud's supersonic projectile beheads her, and Khachi raises her from death by prayer."
"At level 729 she takes the Heir of Wizardry class."
"Over the Blight she rides a storm spell she made and levels the Blight city with four nukes."
"She opposes destroying magic and has Nathan promise not to break Seals."
"By the Ostren war she holds nine mana types."
"In the Ostren war she casts thirteen fusion spells, destroying the Aleph fortress."
"She kills a lightning-bodied Questor by scrambling it with magnetic mana."
"The Maestro offers to teach her 'the true way of the storm'."
"At the Conclave she is the first mortal to fight; she invents aetherwalking and kills Odrin."
"She dreams of seeing the underworld, finding a dragon, and crossing the sky."
"Nine years later she has twins and does wizardry research for Gemore's council."
"She then opens fiery gates across continents and casts near-fusing plasma beams."
